{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "td-01-speed-distance-time-unit-conversions",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Speed, Distance, Time, and Unit Conversions",
    "description": "Build the distance-speed-time relationship and switch safely between hours, minutes, km/hr, m/sec, and m/min.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with a short journey so distance = speed × time has a physical meaning. Reverse the same relationship to find time and speed, then teach unit alignment before arithmetic. Build km/hr ↔ m/sec conversions from the 5/18 and 18/5 factors, use common minute fractions mentally, and finish by comparing speeds written in different units.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 18, Time and Distance. Approved scope: Teach Speed = Distance/Time, Time = Distance/Speed, and Distance = Speed × Time. Cover km/hr to m/sec using ×5/18 and the reverse using ×18/5, hours-minutes conversion, metres per minute, and comparing speeds only after putting them in a common unit. Prepare learners for direct distance/time/speed questions and mixed-unit objective questions."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn the three quantities behind every motion problem.\n\nA journey always links distance, speed and time. If the units match, knowing any two lets you find the third.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A scooter moves at 48 km/hr for 30 minutes.\n\nThirty minutes is half an hour, so it covers half of 48 km:\n\nDistance = 48 × 1/2 = 24 km.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "This is the basic triangle of the chapter:\n\nDistance = Speed × Time\nSpeed = Distance ÷ Time\nTime = Distance ÷ Speed\n\nThe formula is simple. The real check is that the time unit matches the speed unit.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
